sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as Citizen / User
    participant UI as :ChatUI
    participant C as :QAController
    participant L as :LanguageService
    participant R as :RetrievalService
    participant G as :AIModelGateway
    participant M as AI Model Service
    participant V as :AnswerVerifier
    participant H as :ConversationHistory

    U->>UI: enterQuestion(text)
    U->>UI: submitQuestion()
    UI-->>U: showQuestion() + loading indicator
    UI->>C: askQuestion(text)
    Note over C: «Controller»<br/>QAController receives all system events<br/>for this use case, so :ChatUI stays a thin<br/>boundary with no business logic
    C->>L: detectLanguageAndNormalise(text)
    L-->>C: normalisedQuery + language
    Note over L: «Pure Fabrication, High Cohesion»<br/>Khmer/English handling is isolated in one<br/>focused class instead of being spread<br/>across UI and controller
    C->>C: screenGuardrails(question)
    opt question matches a curated Tier-1 answer
        C-->>UI: curated answer, served word-for-word
        UI-->>U: displayAnswer()  (no retrieval, no model call)
    end
    C->>C: checkScope(question)  (government-service questions only)
    C->>R: retrievePassages(query)
    Note right of R: «include» UC-2:<br/>RetrieveOfficialSources
    R-->>C: ranked passages + source metadata
    alt relevant official source found
        C->>G: generateAnswer(question, passages)
        G->>M: model API request (passages only)
        M-->>G: draft answer
        G-->>C: draftAnswer + citedSourceIds
        Note over G: «Indirection, Protected Variations»<br/>The gateway hides the external model<br/>vendor — swapping the AI service changes<br/>only this class
        C->>V: verifyClaims(draftAnswer, passages)
        V-->>C: verified Answer + SourceCitation list
        Note over V: «Creator»<br/>AnswerVerifier works with the data needed<br/>to build the final Answer, so it creates the<br/>Answer object with its citations
        C-->>UI: answer(steps, documents, fees, deadlines, hours)
        UI-->>U: displayAnswer() in the question's language
        UI-->>U: displaySourceCitation()  «include» UC-3
    else no relevant source, or a claim cannot be verified
        C-->>UI: decline(coveredAreas) + escalation option  «extend» UC-4
        UI-->>U: displayDecline() + offer human support
    end
    C->>H: addToRecentConversations(question, answer)
    Note over H: «Information Expert»<br/>ConversationHistory holds past exchanges<br/>(on the citizen's device for the web, in<br/>session memory for Telegram), so it stores<br/>and lists them
